WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.126 --> 00:00:22.032
glanced nervously at the scoreboard in the gym as the seconds ticked away: 58-58.

2
00:00:22.192 --> 00:00:26.235
"Fifteen seconds left in the game," she thought.

3
00:00:26.956 --> 00:00:34.528
Stuart had managed to steal the ball from the Terriers player who'd been racing downcourt.

4
00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:41.494
Now he was dribbling toward the center court line, frantically looking among the players for an opening—probably hoping

5
00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:42.975
to pass the ball to Dirk.

6
00:00:45.197 --> 00:00:48.360
Just then the Terriers point guard lunged at Stuart.

7
00:00:49.961 --> 00:00:51.903
Brooklyn shouted, "Now, Stuart!

8
00:00:52.143 --> 00:00:52.763
Pass it!"

9
00:00:53.824 --> 00:00:55.045
Stuart released the ball.

10
00:00:56.326 --> 00:00:59.849
Dirk leaped into the air to catch it and zipped toward the basket.

11
00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:03.352
"Go, Dirk!"

12
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.561
Brooklyn shouted.

13
00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:06.482
"Three seconds on the clock!"

14
00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:07.682
yelled Marv.

15
00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:10.784
Dirk stopped near the basket.

16
00:01:11.785 --> 00:01:16.387
Then he spun and sprang upward, just as he and Brooklyn had practiced.

17
00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:23.151
The basketball sailed high over the players and then teetered around the basket's rim.

18
00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:27.333
Finally it whooshed through the hoop.

19
00:01:30.855 --> 00:01:32.576
"Yes!" Brooklyn cried.

20
00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:34.476
Whales 60.

21
00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:36.097
Terriers 58.

22
00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:40.338
The final buzzer blared.

23
00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:44.759
The Whales players surrounded Dirk and lifted him high in the air.

24
00:01:44.779 --> 00:01:47.000
"We're number one!"

25
00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.061
shouted Brooklyn, giving Marv a high-five.

26
00:01:50.081 --> 00:01:52.622
"League champions!"

27
00:01:53.862 --> 00:01:55.702
"Woo-hoo!" Marv cried.

28
00:01:55.722 --> 00:01:57.563
"What a coaching staff!"

29
00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:03.337
Marv put Coach Teagan on speakerphone so he could hear the news straight from the team.

30
00:02:03.357 --> 00:02:05.138
"We won!"

31
00:02:05.498 --> 00:02:06.518
the players shouted.

32
00:02:06.538 --> 00:02:09.220
"Way to go, team!"

33
00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.180
Coach said.

34
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.201
"I'll see you at the team party!"

35
00:02:13.201 --> 00:02:16.603
Brooklyn jumped around the court with the team and their happy families.

36
00:02:16.623 --> 00:02:21.225
"Great job, Brooklyn," her dad said.

37
00:02:21.245 --> 00:02:25.106
"Fantastic coaching," her mother chimed in.

38
00:02:25.126 --> 00:02:27.207
"We're very proud of you."

39
00:02:27.848 --> 00:02:28.688
Brooklyn grinned.

40
00:02:29.696 --> 00:02:31.577
"It was such an awesome game."

41
00:02:32.658 --> 00:02:34.199
Marv came up to Brooklyn again.

42
00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:42.043
"I know it was tough coaching your friends," he said, "but you handled it really well, Brooklyn."

43
00:02:42.063 --> 00:02:45.365
"Thanks," Brooklyn said softly.

44
00:02:45.385 --> 00:02:48.266
"Though Jacey might not agree with you."

45
00:02:48.286 --> 00:02:49.967
"What do you mean?"

46
00:02:50.448 --> 00:02:51.668
Brooklyn's mom asked.

47
00:02:52.229 --> 00:02:55.931
Brooklyn blurted out the story about the notes and the sign in the gym.

48
00:02:56.531 --> 00:02:57.852
Her parents were shocked.

49
00:02:59.564 --> 00:03:01.606
"Oh, honey," murmured Mrs.

50
00:03:01.686 --> 00:03:04.008
Robbins. "That's awful."

51
00:03:05.469 --> 00:03:06.470
Marv looked grim.

52
00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.413
"The principal is meeting with Jacey right now.

53
00:03:10.614 --> 00:03:12.816
She will have to sit out next basketball season.

54
00:03:13.456 --> 00:03:16.139
Neither the school nor the team will tolerate bullying."

55
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.002
The Whales started gathering their basketball gear.

56
00:03:22.645 --> 00:03:25.567
Then everyone headed to Brooklyn's house for the party.

57
00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.102
"Whoa! That's some cake!"

58
00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:31.563
Dirk burst out.

59
00:03:32.203 --> 00:03:33.144
Brooklyn beamed.

60
00:03:35.206 --> 00:03:40.491
The big orange cake, shaped like a basketball, sat on a platter in the center of the dining

61
00:03:40.531 --> 00:03:41.171
room table.

62
00:03:42.092 --> 00:03:46.216
On top of the cake was a huge whale made of blue frosting.

63
00:03:46.236 --> 00:03:48.418
"Mom and I made it this morning!"

64
00:03:48.838 --> 00:03:49.799
she said proudly.

65
00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:54.984
Soon Coach Teagan and his wife arrived, rolling in a large stroller.

66
00:03:57.368 --> 00:03:59.749
Three tiny babies lay inside.

67
00:04:04.011 --> 00:04:08.452
While everybody gushed over the cute babies, Brooklyn ran upstairs to get something.

68
00:04:08.472 --> 00:04:12.534
"I hope the triplets like basketball."

69
00:04:13.254 --> 00:04:17.076
She gave Coach and his wife three small plush orange basketballs.

70
00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:20.677
Mrs. Teagan placed a ball next to each infant.

71
00:04:20.697 --> 00:04:25.259
"In this family everybody loves basketball!"

72
00:04:25.839 --> 00:04:28.965
The team ate pizza and reviewed the championship game.

73
00:04:28.985 --> 00:04:33.268
"That was an unbelievable pass, Stuart," Marv said.

74
00:04:33.288 --> 00:04:35.089
"Perfect timing."

75
00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.631
Stuart shrugged and looked at Brooklyn.

76
00:04:37.651 --> 00:04:40.613
"I just followed the assistant coach's instructions."

77
00:04:40.633 --> 00:04:43.375
"Me too," added Dirk.

78
00:04:44.015 --> 00:04:45.857
"She's the one who taught me the Jedi Jump."

79
00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:48.839
Brooklyn felt a surge of pride.

80
00:04:48.859 --> 00:04:52.441
"It's easy to be a good coach when you've got great players!"

81
00:04:53.542 --> 00:04:58.284
The team watched a slide show of photos from the Whales' season that Brooklyn's dad had made on

82
00:04:58.324 --> 00:04:59.005
his computer.

83
00:05:00.765 --> 00:05:02.146
Mrs. Robbins stood up.

84
00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:04.586
"Time to cut the cake!"

85
00:05:05.687 --> 00:05:07.087
Just then the doorbell rang.

86
00:05:07.107 --> 00:05:11.348
"I'll get it," called Brooklyn's dad.

87
00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:20.611
hello, Jacey," Brooklyn heard him say, sounding surprised.

88
00:05:21.771 --> 00:05:23.592
Everyone instantly fell silent.

89
00:05:24.348 --> 00:05:27.150
Jacey stood awkwardly in the doorway for a moment.

90
00:05:27.811 --> 00:05:29.152
"Come in," Mr.

91
00:05:29.192 --> 00:05:30.553
Robbins said quietly.

92
00:05:30.573 --> 00:05:36.857
"Jacey, we're sorry you chose to miss the second half of the game," Marv said.

93
00:05:37.658 --> 00:05:39.139
Jacey looked down at her feet.

94
00:05:39.159 --> 00:05:43.202
"I'm sorry I missed it too," she said in a small voice.

95
00:05:43.222 --> 00:05:45.603
"But I'm glad the Whales won."

96
00:05:46.244 --> 00:05:47.705
She raised her eyes to Brooklyn.

97
00:05:47.725 --> 00:05:49.206
"Can I talk to you?

98
00:05:50.026 --> 00:05:51.808
Outside?" "Sure."

99
00:05:52.588 --> 00:05:56.810
Brooklyn put down her plate of uneaten cake and went outside with Jacey.

100
00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:05.455
The girls stood together on the front porch.

101
00:06:05.475 --> 00:06:08.457
"I have to tell you the truth."

102
00:06:09.397 --> 00:06:10.978
Jacey had tears in her eyes.

103
00:06:10.998 --> 00:06:12.339
"I did it.

104
00:06:13.119 --> 00:06:14.180
I wrote those notes.

105
00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.621
Brooklyn, I'm so sorry!"

106
00:06:17.581 --> 00:06:19.102
Brooklyn stared at her friend.

107
00:06:19.122 --> 00:06:22.004
"I still can't believe it," she said.

108
00:06:22.716 --> 00:06:24.157
"Why would you do that to me?"

109
00:06:24.177 --> 00:06:25.898
"I was jealous.

110
00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:29.321
I used to be a starter on the team," Jacey said.

111
00:06:29.341 --> 00:06:33.804
"But then Coach and Marv started leaving me on the bench sometimes.

112
00:06:34.504 --> 00:06:37.026
Plus, you were getting all of the attention."

113
00:06:37.046 --> 00:06:40.128
"Huh?" Brooklyn furrowed her brow.

114
00:06:40.828 --> 00:06:41.669
"What attention?"

115
00:06:41.689 --> 00:06:44.651
"From Marv and from the team.

116
00:06:45.031 --> 00:06:45.852
Dirk too."

117
00:06:46.913 --> 00:06:48.274
Jacey's face turned red.

118
00:06:48.294 --> 00:06:51.576
"I think he likes you better than he likes me."

119
00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:56.373
"I just wanted to help Marv and the team," Brooklyn said.

120
00:06:56.393 --> 00:06:59.555
"I can't play basketball like you can, Jacey.

121
00:07:00.475 --> 00:07:04.017
I know I'm not a very good coach yet, but I'll keep working on it."

122
00:07:04.037 --> 00:07:06.958
"You're already a good coach, Brooklyn.

123
00:07:07.698 --> 00:07:08.498
Marv knows it.

124
00:07:08.738 --> 00:07:09.619
Dirk knows it."

125
00:07:10.299 --> 00:07:11.700
Jacey smiled sadly.

126
00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.480
"I know it too.

127
00:07:14.181 --> 00:07:16.762
You'll definitely coach in the pro league someday.

128
00:07:17.222 --> 00:07:18.142
I'm sure of it."

129
00:07:19.323 --> 00:07:22.004
There was a pause as the two girls looked at each other.

130
00:07:23.356 --> 00:07:24.757
Jacey let out a sigh.

131
00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:28.540
"I'm so sorry for hurting you, Brooklyn.

132
00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.082
Writing those notes was a stupid and mean thing to do.

133
00:07:32.763 --> 00:07:33.643
Will you forgive me?"

134
00:07:34.604 --> 00:07:36.025
Brooklyn nodded slowly.

135
00:07:36.045 --> 00:07:38.667
"I think so," she replied.

136
00:07:39.428 --> 00:07:40.328
Then she shrugged.

137
00:07:40.348 --> 00:07:41.829
"Who knows.

138
00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.971
Maybe you'll even play on my pro team someday!"

139
00:07:44.991 --> 00:07:48.554
"Maybe." Jacey grinned.

140
00:07:49.254 --> 00:07:51.216
"Only if you teach me that Jedi Jump.

141
00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.621
I heard everyone talking about it."

142
00:07:53.641 --> 00:07:56.884
"Sure. I'll show you how to do it right now.

143
00:07:57.484 --> 00:07:58.605
Let's get a basketball."

144
00:08:00.907 --> 00:08:04.349
Brooklyn rushed forward—and stumbled over her own feet.

145
00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:09.353
Jacey grabbed Brooklyn's arm before Brooklyn toppled down the steps.

146
00:08:09.373 --> 00:08:12.615
"Whew! You saved me!"

147
00:08:12.995 --> 00:08:13.716
Brooklyn said.

148
00:08:13.736 --> 00:08:15.217
"Thanks, Jacey."

149
00:08:15.237 --> 00:08:19.360
"It was the least I could do," Jacey said softly.

150
00:08:20.276 --> 00:08:25.801
The girls began shooting hoops in the driveway, and soon the rest of the Whales came outside and

151
00:08:25.841 --> 00:08:26.381
joined them.

152
00:08:29.884 --> 00:08:33.147
A few of them glanced uncertainly between Jacey and Brooklyn.

153
00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:35.549
"Everything okay?"

154
00:08:36.209 --> 00:08:37.890
Dirk asked Brooklyn quietly.

155
00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:40.853
Brooklyn nodded and dribbled toward the basket.

156
00:08:42.854 --> 00:08:44.396
She missed an easy shot.

157
00:08:46.517 --> 00:08:49.480
Dirk grabbed the rebound and passed the ball back to her.

158
00:08:51.628 --> 00:08:52.249
"Try again."

159
00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:54.570
Brooklyn dribbled fast.

160
00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:59.373
"Come on, Robbins," she coached herself.

161
00:09:00.054 --> 00:09:01.154
"Aim with your arms!"

162
00:09:02.435 --> 00:09:04.156
She lined up for another throw.

163
00:09:04.857 --> 00:09:08.459
Whoosh! The basketball dropped neatly through the net.

164
00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:12.482
Then Brooklyn heard another "whoosh."

165
00:09:13.463 --> 00:09:17.085
This time it was her team, cheering loudly for her.

166
00:09:17.105 --> 00:09:19.407
"Whales Whoosh!"

167
00:09:20.027 --> 00:09:21.188
they cried together.
